#==============================================================================================
#
#   interpolation_4 - CSS interpolation: shadows, mixed numeric values and the value types
#
#   DESCRIPTION:
#       Port of Libraries/LibWeb/CSS/Interpolation.cpp (lines 1378-1555 and 1556-1776), by
#       region p4a: the interpolation of shadow lists (padding with blank shadows), the value
#       type of a numeric style value, the interpolation of mixed numeric values (a
#       percentage-dimension mix or a calc() of both), and interpolate_value_impl: values of
#       different types or calculated ones are mixed, others are interpolated by their type.
#       Its longer cases (basic shapes, font styles, radial sizes, superellipses, value lists)
#       are functions of part 5. length_percentage_or_auto_to_style_value (lines 1540-1554) is
#       a template no code instantiates, so it is not ported.
#
#       Copyright (c) 2018-2023, Andreas Kling <andreas@ladybird.org>
#       Copyright (c) 2021-2025, Sam Atkins <sam@ladybird.org>
